/-!
# Balog-Szemeredi-Gowers and dense bipartite paths

This file was automatically generated by Codex.

The classical energy-to-small-difference-set argument for finite subsets of
arbitrary abelian groups. Its combinatorial prerequisite is a dependent
random choice argument producing many four-step paths between every pair
in a large vertex set of a dense finite bipartite graph. Repeated vertices
are allowed. Proper edge colors recover a path from its starting vertex.

The intended quantitative conclusion is the source exponent ten: additive
energy at least |A|^3/K yields a subset of size at least c|A|/K whose
difference set has size at most C K^10 times the subset size. The proof is
developed in forward source order; no unproved target is assumed.

Verified source: blueprint/formalization_blueprint.tex, lem:four-paths,
lines 668-680, and lem:BSG, lines 683-698. All statements and supporting
definitions use only Mathlib and this module. Mathlib's Finset.addEnergy
is the standard additive-energy quantity used by the consuming theorem.
